      "purpose": "An open-source, low-cost, high fidelty flexible laryngoscope designed and reviewed by biomedical engineers and board-certified otolaryngologists for use in resource-limited settings.",
      "description": "An open-source, low-cost, high fidelty flexible laryngoscope designed and reviewed by biomedical engineers and board-certified otolaryngologists for use in resource-limited settings. The device consists of a distal-chip camera, spring bending tip, handle housing the control mechanism and electronics, and flexible PEBAX-coated silicone sheath housing the camera and control wires. An external monitor provides real-time visualization and ability to store data. The spring bending tip is robust, simple to manufacture, and customizable in stiffness, length, and diameter to tune angulation and force.",
